   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3747"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa byams pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person3758"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">vasubandhu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon dbyig gnyen</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6119</idno><idno type="APIS">3758</idno></person><person xml:id="person3798"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">parahitabhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gzhan la phan pa bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pa ra hi ta</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01" notAfter="1060-12-31">after 1000 before 1060</birth><death notBefore="1080-01-01" notAfter="1140-12-31">after 1080 before 1140</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8225</idno><idno type="APIS">3798</idno></person><person xml:id="person3800"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sajjana</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">paN+Di ta sa dza na</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01" notAfter="1072-12-31">after 1000 before 1072</birth><death notBefore="1076-01-01" notAfter="1099-12-31">after 1076 before 1099</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4920</idno><idno type="APIS">3800</idno><note type="comment">Grand-son of Ratnavajra (ID:7726) ([BAQ9MH4T]: 406, n. 2).</note></person><person xml:id="person3883"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">grags pa rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྲགས་པ་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><birth notBefore="1100-01-01" notAfter="1241-12-31">after 1100 before 1241</birth><death notBefore="1115-01-01" notAfter="1321-12-31">after 1115 before 1321</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">3883</idno></person><person xml:id="person3977"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mchims nam mkha' grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མཆིམས་ནམ་མཁའ་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'chims nam mkha' grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong nam mkha' grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shAkya'i btsun pa mchims</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phyims nam mkha' grags</persName><birth notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1210-12-31">1210</birth><death notBefore="1285-12-11" notAfter="1285-12-11">1285-12-11</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1060</idno><idno type="APIS">3977</idno><note type="comment">Seventh abbot of sNar thang monastery (ID:4411). On his dates see [2X2E3882]: 260, n. 146.</note></person><person xml:id="person4006"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རིགས་པའི་རལ་གྲི</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs ral</persName><birth notBefore="1227-01-01" notAfter="1227-12-31">1227</birth><death notBefore="1305-08-29" notAfter="1305-08-29">1305-08-29</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1217</idno><idno type="APIS">4006</idno><note type="comment">On his career, see [KHA9ZVGP]: 3-8.&#13;
The dates 1227-1305 are known from the biography (see work (ID:7016)) composed by his student bSam gtan bzang po (ID:4005) ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).&#13;
His name in religion was Dar ma rgyal mtshan or Chos kyi rgyal mtshan ([FZ6N88AU]: 406) - the name Chos kyi rgyal mtshan is given as his "real name" (mtshan dngos) in a homage by Rong ston ([KM47ZZDJ]: 657 and n. 62). &#13;
The majority of the colophons of his works name him "bCom ldan ral gri," a few "Rigs/Rig pa’i ral gri" or just "Ral gri." Schwabland's discussion of the variants “Rigs pa” and “Rig pa” does not come to a definite conclusion as to which is the correct spelling ([CTQMVBPR]: 2-3).&#13;
He was born as the son of a local wealthy headman, the fourth of five sons and his birth is reported to have been foretold by Śākyaśrībhadra (ID:6418) when he was invited by Ral gri's paternal uncle ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).</note></person><person xml:id="person4062"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">skyi ston shAkya 'bum</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">སྐྱི་སྟོན་ཤཱཀྱ་འབུམ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">skyi ston shag 'bum</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1200-12-31">1200</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P5741</idno><idno type="APIS">4062</idno></person><person xml:id="person4092"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo gros grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བློ་གྲོས་གྲགས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P0RK1758</idno><idno type="APIS">4092</idno></person><person xml:id="person4097"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpang lo tsA ba blo gros brtan pa</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དཔང་ལོ་ཙཱ་བ་བློ་གྲོས་བརྟན་པ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpang blo gros brtan pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">btsun chung lu gu</persName><birth notBefore="1276-01-01" notAfter="1276-12-31">1276</birth><death notBefore="1342-01-01" notAfter="1342-12-31">1342</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2085</idno><idno type="APIS">4097</idno><note type="comment">A short biography from the Shel dkar chos 'byung is translated in [N35FPQ6L]: 62-70. It gives a fire-male-mouse year (1276) as birth-date, and Gyam in Zur rtso as its birthplace. He took novice vows when he was five years old at 'Brog rdo gling, and was ordained at seven.</note></person><person xml:id="person4125"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gha rung pa lha'i rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྷ་རུང་པ་ལྷའི་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><birth notBefore="1319-01-01" notAfter="1319-12-31">1319</birth><death notBefore="1401-01-01" notAfter="1401-12-31">1401</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2414</idno><idno type="APIS">4125</idno><note type="comment">Scholar associated with the Jo nang pa.</note></person><person xml:id="person4128"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa bzang ma ti paN chen blo gros rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ས་བཟང་མ་ཏི་པཎ་ཆེན་བློ་གྲོས་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bod kyi paNDita ma ti rha ja shri bha dra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bod kyi pandita 'jam dbyangs blo gros</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa bzang 'phags pa blo gros rgyal mtshan</persName><birth notBefore="1294-01-01" notAfter="1294-12-31">1294</birth><death notBefore="1376-01-01" notAfter="1376-12-31">1376</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P151</idno><idno type="APIS">4128</idno></person><person xml:id="person4212"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'chim ston don 'grub</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཆིམ་སྟོན་དོན་འགྲུབ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'chims ston don grub</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mchims ston don grub</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P0RK1760</idno><idno type="APIS">4212</idno></person><person xml:id="person4213"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dol po pa shes rab rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དོལ་པོ་པ་ཤེས་རབ་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><birth notBefore="1292-01-01" notAfter="1292-12-31">1292</birth><death notBefore="1361-01-01" notAfter="1361-12-31">1361</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>T